\fs28\b Alpine Ascents - Assumptions\b0\par
\fs22\par
\b Visitor count\b0\par
The visitor number starts at 1,200 and is stored in this browser's localStorage. sessionStorage prevents more than one increment per browser session. It is a local estimate, not a global visitor total. If browser storage is blocked, the site remains usable and the seed value is shown.\par
\par
\b Location and time ticker\b0\par
The ticker uses the visitor's local clock and requests location through the browser Geolocation API. Location is permission-dependent. If access is denied, times out, or is unsupported, the ticker says Location unavailable. A free OpenStreetMap Nominatim reverse-geocoding request attempts to name the place; rounded latitude and longitude are used when lookup fails. Internet access is required for reverse lookup.\par
\par
\b Map\b0\par
The Records page uses an embedded OpenStreetMap map. No client-side map library is installed. Map tiles require internet access.\par
\par
\b Content and images\b0\par
Mountaineering copy is maintained in project JSON and is for general education, not a substitute for qualified instruction, emergency services, or current local conditions. Page imagery is loaded from Unsplash URLs. Verify local access, permits, forecasts, and route conditions before travel.\par
\par
\b Environment\b0\par
The application is a client-rendered React and Vite site. Nested route refreshes require a static host configured to return index.html for application routes.\par
}